  "id": "dissonance",
  "term": "dissonance",
  "definition": "Dissonance is a quality in music marked by greater tonal clash or instability that can evoke strong emotional intensity. In this study, it was linked less with pleasure than consonance, but more with feelings such as power and awe until it became extremely pronounced, at which point those responses dropped.",
